{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Authentication - Okta Authentication Through a Proxy Chain [table]",
	"Description": "Groups authentications where the immediate client address and the first hop of Okta's request IP chain disagree, which means the request came through a proxy. A proxy in front of authentication hides the real origin, and the accounts and device tokens sharing one proxy tell you how much traffic is behind it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_multiple_okta_user_auth_events_with_same_device_token_hash_behind_a_proxy/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "6dec7f8b-d4b2-501b-b6aa-54af34b6c387",
	"SearchReference": "90cb4212-082a-5fc1-88ac-b8eb8cd999a6"
}